course: dictionary
lesson: 917
title: Blanket: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Blanket is a good example. It can be a warm cloth you sleep under, a thick covering of something, or a verb meaning to cover completely.
explain: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air; carbon dioxide traps heat like a blanket, so even a small rise warms the planet.» Here a blanket is not a bed cover. The words like a blanket show a comparison: the gas works like a blanket around the Earth.
explain: Try the swap test. Put a meaning such as «thick covering» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. In «Venus's thick atmosphere (its blanket of gas) traps heat», the brackets explain the word for you, so the context does the work.
explain: Blanket can also describe something. A blanket rule covers every case, so it is not just for one situation. When you meet blanket in a new sentence, read the words around it first, then decide which meaning fits.
fact: A blanket is a large piece of warm cloth used to cover you in bed or keep you warm.
fact: A blanket of something is a thick covering of it, like «a blanket of snow».
fact: To blanket means to cover something completely.
fact: A blanket keeps you warm because it traps air and stops heat escaping; it does not make heat itself.
fact: A fire blanket smothers a small pan fire in the kitchen, but never throw water on burning oil.
exercise: «The town woke under a blanket of snow.» What does blanket of snow mean? | *A thick covering of snow | A warm cloth to wrap the town in | A long white road | A sledge for children
exercise: «Red pandas wrap their thick tail around themselves like a blanket.» What is the tail doing? | Making a loud noise | *Wrapping round them to keep them warm | Sliding down a steep branch | Turning into fur
exercise: «Fog will blanket the valley by morning.» What does blanket mean here? | *To cover completely | To pull a warm cloth off a bed | To run very fast | To shine brightly
test: «A blanket rule is one that covers every case.» What does a blanket rule cover? | No cases at all | *Every case | Only the cases on Fridays | Only one case
test: Which job is a fire blanket for? | Keeping a sleeping cat warm | *Smothering a small pan fire in the kitchen | Building a den in a tree | Throwing water on burning oil
exam: «A blanket keeps you warm because…» Why does a blanket keep you warm? | It makes heat inside itself | It is made of ice | *It traps air and stops heat escaping | It pulls cold out of the room
